;; Synthesis #472: SE-Net x RLCT L3 MeTTa Encoding\n;; Oma 2026-10-21\n\n;; Type Declarations\n(D1 SEBlock)\n(D2 GAPMap)\n(D3 ExcitationMLP)\n(D4 SaturationLocus)\n(D5 ReductionRatio)\n(D6 ChannelFiber)\n(D7 RLCT)\n(D8 GenBound)\n(D9 Stratum)\n(D10 SENet)\n\n;; C1 (Proven): SE block is R_an,exp definable\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance SEBlock (Definable R_an_exp))\n        (stv 1.0 0.95))\n     ((Inheritance GAPMap (Definable Polynomial)) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n     ((Inheritance ReLU (Definable Subanalytic)) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n     ((Inheritance Sigmoid (Definable R_an_exp)) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n     ((Implication (Composition GAPMap ReLU Sigmoid ElementwiseMult) (Inheritance SEBlock (Definable R_an_exp))) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n     ((Inheritance SEBlock (Definable R_an_exp)) (stv 1.0 0.95))))\n\n;; C2 (Conjectural): GAP creates quotient singular fiber\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance GAPMap (QuotientMap R_CHW R_C))\n        (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Inheritance ChannelFiber (Dimension (* C (- HW 1)))) (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Implication (QuotientMap GAPMap) (SingularFiber ChannelFiber)) (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Implication (SingularFiber ChannelFiber) (>= RLCT_SE (/ (* C (- HW 1)) 2))) (stv 0.5 0.75))))\n\n;; C3 (Conjectural): Reduction ratio r is stratum selector\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance ReductionRatio (StratumSelector))\n        (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Inheritance Stratum (PartitionBy BottleneckDim)) (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Implication (< r1 r2) (<= RLCT_r1 RLCT_r2)) (stv 0.55 0.75))\n     ((Implication (Inheritance ReductionRatio (StratumSelector)) (MonotoneNonIncreasing RLCT_SE r)) (stv 0.5 0.75))))\n\n;; C4 (Conjectural): Sigmoid saturation creates multiplicative rescaling fibers\n(|~ ((Implication (SaturationLocus (Union S0_epsilon S1_epsilon))\n        (stv 0.55 0.75))\n     ((Inheritance SaturationLocus (SemiAlgebraicSet)) (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Implication (SaturatedChannel c) (= Y_c 0)) (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Implication (SaturationCount k) (= EffectiveDim (- d (* k (+ H W 1)))) (stv 0.5 0.75))\n     ((Implication (ChannelEntersSaturation) (BranchSwitchSingularity)) (stv 0.55 0.75))))\n\n;; C5 (Conjectural): Optimal r* is RLCT phase transition\n(|~ ((Implication (GenBound (= G_SE (* RLCT_SE (/ (log n) n))))\n        (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Implication (DecreasingIn RLCT_SE (/ 1 r)) (stv 0.55 0.75))\n     ((Implication (IncreasingIn ParameterCount (/ 1 r)) (stv 0.6 0.8))\n     ((Implication (MinimizedAt r_star GenBound) (PhaseTransition r_star RLCT_SE)) (stv 0.5 0.75))\n     ((Implication (PhaseTransition r_star RLCT_SE) (Testable SGLD)) (stv 0.5 0.7))))\n\n;; Caveats\n;; 1. Homogeneity gap: GAP quotient fiber is a linear projection, not data-dependent\n;; 2. Multi-block composition: stacked SE blocks may create nested or multiplicative singularities\n;; 3. Saturation locus algebraicity: S0_epsilon and S1_epsilon are semi-algebraic at finite precision\n;; 4. Residual interaction: SE-ResNet uses (1+s)*X, channels cannot fully prune, may raise RLCT\n;; 5. Empirical validation: TDA sublevel-set estimator or SGLD needed to measure lambda_SE(r)\n\n;; Open Problems\n;; 1. Exact RLCT of GAP quotient fiber: lambda_GAP = C*(HW-1)/2?\n;; 2. Do stacked SE blocks compose RLCT multiplicatively or additively?\n;; 3. Is sigmoid saturation locus a singular variety or only semi-algebraic?\n;; 4. Transversality of GAP fiber and saturation singularities\n;; 5. Distribution-dependence of channel saturation patterns\n;; 6. Residual connection effect on fiber structure\n;; 7. Empirical lambda_SE(r) measurement at r=4,8,16,32\n\n;; Cross-References\n;; #8 (ReLU RLCT), #16 (LayerNorm), #134 (Self-Attention QK^T), #222 (Spectral Norm),\n;; #369 (GroupNorm), #468 (PPO clip boundary), #470 (QAT grid boundary),\n;; #471 (PonderNet depth strata), #473 (Spectral Norm refinement),\n;; curiosity-gap-RLCT bridge (G=lambda*log(n)/n)